Switch 2 titles send their rumble with HID command 214 (SendNx2VibrationValues), a batch of device
handles and HD rumble values in two pointer buffers; Mario Kart World sends one every 5 ms. It was
an accept-and-drop stub, so those titles never rumbled. The values are decoded as ProsperoEden does
(u16 flags, the applet resource user id, then the handles and values, the Switch 1 value layout)
and go through the same per-device path as 206 SendVibrationValues, so they reach the emulated
controllers' vibration. Batches that cannot be played are dropped, never failed back to the game,
as the stub did; logging stays at Debug.

